"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunklinux_cleanup_docs||=[]).push([[665],{43408(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"desktop-1.0.5","metadata":{"permalink":"/feed/desktop-1.0.5","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-26-desktop-1-0-5.md","title":"Desktop 1.0.5","description":"The app speaks ten languages, and a signed-in account keeps the choice on every computer and in its emails.","date":"2026-11-26T16:40:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"desktop-1.0.5","title":"Desktop 1.0.5","description":"The app speaks ten languages, and a signed-in account keeps the choice on every computer and in its emails.","date":"2026-11-26T16:40"},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"Desktop 1.0.4","permalink":"/feed/desktop-1.0.4"}},"content":"The app speaks ten languages: English, Simplified Chinese, Hindi, Spanish, Arabic, French, Brazilian Portuguese,\\nRussian, Japanese and Urdu. Pick one in Settings \u2192 General \u2192 Language.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nSigned in, the choice follows your account to your other computers, and account emails arrive in it. Arabic and\\nUrdu read right to left, with paths and commands still left to right. Help has More from Zaions and About the\\ndeveloper. The bundled command line is still 2.1.1, and the app updates itself from 1.0.4."},{"id":"desktop-1.0.4","metadata":{"permalink":"/feed/desktop-1.0.4","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-22-desktop-1-0-4.md","title":"Desktop 1.0.4","description":"The AppImage adds itself to the applications menu, and the window shows the linux-cleanup icon.","date":"2026-11-22T14:45:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"desktop-1.0.4","title":"Desktop 1.0.4","description":"The AppImage adds itself to the applications menu, and the window shows the linux-cleanup icon.","date":"2026-11-22T14:45"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Desktop 1.0.5","permalink":"/feed/desktop-1.0.5"},"nextItem":{"title":"Desktop 1.0.3","permalink":"/feed/desktop-1.0.3"}},"content":"The AppImage now adds itself to your applications menu, with its icon, the first time it runs, and keeps that\\nentry pointing at wherever the file lives. The open window and the dock show the linux-cleanup icon instead of a\\nblank one. The .deb already did this. Nothing changed in what the app cleans. The app updates itself."},{"id":"desktop-1.0.3","metadata":{"permalink":"/feed/desktop-1.0.3","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-22-desktop-1-0-3.md","title":"Desktop 1.0.3","description":"Ships with the command line 2.1.1 and current libraries.","date":"2026-11-22T12:16:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"desktop-1.0.3","title":"Desktop 1.0.3","description":"Ships with the command line 2.1.1 and current libraries.","date":"2026-11-22T12:16"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Desktop 1.0.4","permalink":"/feed/desktop-1.0.4"},"nextItem":{"title":"CLI 2.1.1","permalink":"/feed/cli-2.1.1"}},"content":"The app now ships with the command line 2.1.1 and current libraries. Nothing changed in what it cleans. The app\\nupdates itself."},{"id":"cli-2.1.1","metadata":{"permalink":"/feed/cli-2.1.1","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-22-cli-2-1-1.md","title":"CLI 2.1.1","description":"The help, version and About screens point to the website, this manual and the desktop download.","date":"2026-11-22T12:01:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"cli-2.1.1","title":"CLI 2.1.1","description":"The help, version and About screens point to the website, this manual and the desktop download.","date":"2026-11-22T12:01"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Desktop 1.0.3","permalink":"/feed/desktop-1.0.3"},"nextItem":{"title":"Desktop 1.0.2","permalink":"/feed/desktop-1.0.2"}},"content":"`--help`, `--version` and the menu\'s About box now point to the website, this manual and the desktop app\'s\\ndownload page. The About box also says plainly that the script reads the public release record once at start.\\nNothing changed in what any mode removes. Run it with `npx -y linux-cleanup@2.1.1 --version`."},{"id":"desktop-1.0.2","metadata":{"permalink":"/feed/desktop-1.0.2","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-22-desktop-1-0-2.md","title":"Desktop 1.0.2","description":"Clearer wording on the Updates screen and a working check command on the errors screen.","date":"2026-11-22T09:40:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"desktop-1.0.2","title":"Desktop 1.0.2","description":"Clearer wording on the Updates screen and a working check command on the errors screen.","date":"2026-11-22T09:40"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"CLI 2.1.1","permalink":"/feed/cli-2.1.1"},"nextItem":{"title":"Desktop 1.0.1","permalink":"/feed/desktop-1.0.1"}},"content":"Clearer wording on the Updates screen, and the errors screen now copies a command that works:\\n`npx -y linux-cleanup --self-test`. The app updates itself."},{"id":"desktop-1.0.1","metadata":{"permalink":"/feed/desktop-1.0.1","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-22-desktop-1-0-1.md","title":"Desktop 1.0.1","description":"Error reports with no paths or file names, a walkthrough with real screens, a Get linux-cleanup page and steadier page tours.","date":"2026-11-22T07:40:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"desktop-1.0.1","title":"Desktop 1.0.1","description":"Error reports with no paths or file names, a walkthrough with real screens, a Get linux-cleanup page and steadier page tours.","date":"2026-11-22T07:40"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Desktop 1.0.2","permalink":"/feed/desktop-1.0.2"},"nextItem":{"title":"Desktop 1.0.0","permalink":"/feed/desktop-1.0.0"}},"content":"Error reports reach us without paths or file names, the walkthrough shows real screens, and Help has a Get\\nlinux-cleanup page listing every place it runs.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nPage tours keep each step in view as you move through them. The app updated itself from 1.0.0. See\\n[installing the desktop app](/desktop/install)."},{"id":"desktop-1.0.0","metadata":{"permalink":"/feed/desktop-1.0.0","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-21-desktop-1-0-0.md","title":"Desktop 1.0.0","description":"The first desktop release, an AppImage and .deb for x86_64 Linux bundling CLI 2.1.0.","date":"2026-11-21T14:00:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"desktop-1.0.0","title":"Desktop 1.0.0","description":"The first desktop release, an AppImage and .deb for x86_64 Linux bundling CLI 2.1.0.","date":"2026-11-21T14:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Desktop 1.0.1","permalink":"/feed/desktop-1.0.1"},"nextItem":{"title":"CLI 2.1.0","permalink":"/feed/cli-2.1.0"}},"content":"The first desktop release: the all-safe cleanup in a window, with a dry run before every real run and a receipt\\nafter it.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nAppImage and .deb for x86_64 Linux, bundling CLI 2.1.0. It updates itself from signed releases. Start with\\n[installing the desktop app](/desktop/install)."},{"id":"cli-2.1.0","metadata":{"permalink":"/feed/cli-2.1.0","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-21-cli-2-1-0.md","title":"CLI 2.1.0","description":"--json-events streams local, versioned JSON events for --scan and non-interactive all-safe runs, dry runs included.","date":"2026-11-21T12:00:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"cli-2.1.0","title":"CLI 2.1.0","description":"--json-events streams local, versioned JSON events for --scan and non-interactive all-safe runs, dry runs included.","date":"2026-11-21T12:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Desktop 1.0.0","permalink":"/feed/desktop-1.0.0"},"nextItem":{"title":"CLI 2.0.1","permalink":"/feed/cli-2.0.1"}},"content":"`--json-events` streams local, versioned JSON events for `--scan` and non-interactive `--all-safe --yes`.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nAdding `--dry-run` to all-safe reports proposed paths without deleting them. The stream can contain full local\\npaths, so keep it on the machine. The [JSON events reference](/reference/json-events) and the [changelog](/changelog)\\nhave the details."},{"id":"cli-2.0.1","metadata":{"permalink":"/feed/cli-2.0.1","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-21-cli-2-0-1.md","title":"CLI 2.0.1","description":"The README lists every place linux-cleanup is released. No change to what the script does.","date":"2026-11-21T10:00:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"cli-2.0.1","title":"CLI 2.0.1","description":"The README lists every place linux-cleanup is released. No change to what the script does.","date":"2026-11-21T10:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"CLI 2.1.0","permalink":"/feed/cli-2.1.0"},"nextItem":{"title":"CLI 2.0.0","permalink":"/feed/cli-2.0.0"}},"content":"The README lists every place linux-cleanup is released. No change to what the script does."},{"id":"cli-2.0.0","metadata":{"permalink":"/feed/cli-2.0.0","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-10-cli-2-0-0.md","title":"CLI 2.0.0","description":"linux-cleanup 2.0.0 adds --dry-run, a release-record check on start and --refresh-app.","date":"2026-11-10T12:00:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"cli-2.0.0","title":"CLI 2.0.0","description":"linux-cleanup 2.0.0 adds --dry-run, a release-record check on start and --refresh-app.","date":"2026-11-10T12:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"CLI 2.0.1","permalink":"/feed/cli-2.0.1"}},"content":"Added `--dry-run`, a public release-record check on start, and `--refresh-app` for the persistent CLI copy.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nNormal release notices allow the first run and block from the next start; urgent notices block an older copy at\\nonce. Offline runs continue. A dry run does not remove cleanup targets or change settings, though it may write a\\nlocal log and update-check state. Read the [changelog](/changelog) for the full entry."}]}}')}}]);